# 🔋 Renewable & Grid Energy Balancing System

An intelligent power management system that automatically switches between solar energy and grid supply based on real-time generation and load demand, ensuring efficient, reliable, and uninterrupted power delivery.

## 📌 Overview

This project focuses on optimizing energy utilization by prioritizing renewable energy sources while maintaining seamless fallback to the grid when required.

The system continuously monitors solar power generation, load demand, and system conditions. Based on these inputs, it dynamically switches between power sources using control logic and relay-based switching.

## ⚙️ Features

- 🌞 Smart Source Switching  
  Automatically selects solar power when sufficient and switches to grid during low generation or high demand.

- 📊 Real-Time Monitoring  
  Measures voltage, current, and load conditions continuously.

- 🔄 Seamless Transition  
  No manual intervention required; ensures uninterrupted power supply.

- ⚡ Relay-Based Protection  
  Safe switching between sources with isolation and protection against backflow.

- 🧠 Efficient Energy Utilization  
  Maximizes renewable energy usage and reduces dependency on grid power.

## 🧠 Working Principle

1. The system continuously measures solar panel output (voltage and current) and load demand.  
2. The controller processes this data and decides the power source:  
   - If solar power is sufficient → load is powered by solar  
   - If insufficient → system switches to grid supply  
3. A relay module performs safe switching between sources.  
4. Protection logic ensures no overlap between sources and stable operation.

